defklown wrote:
>
> Are the following two statements true? Attacking a peaceful creature,
> regardless of chaotic/neutral/lawful, results in a decrease in
> alignment. Killing a previously peaceful creature, regardless of
> chaotic/neutral/lawful, results in a great decrease in alignment.
>
> If so, does that mean that if I want to kill, say, a watch captain,
> there's no way to do so without lowering my alignment?
>
> Also, does anyone know _exactly_ how sacrificing for artifacts works?

Among other things there is no chance whatsoever until a list
of stats are non-negative.  You have to be reconciled.

> As in, does anyone know how to calculate the chance of getting an
> artifact, based on your luck,

Luck needs to be non-negative I think.  Zero though max does
not matter.  So continue to sac until reconciled and then keep
going.

> your god's anger,

The responses are mollified and inadequate.  There is no chance at
all while anger is non-zero so sac bigger and bigger monsters
until then.

> your alignment,

Once you are reconciled you will know your alignment is positive.

> the
> difficulty of the monster whose corpse is being sacrificed,

Matters greatly for anger (small monsters have no effect), matters
linearly for prayer timeout (a 10 point monster has 1/10th the
benefit of a 100 point monster), is completely irrelevant once
reconciled (once reconciled a next is as likely/unlikely to give
an artifact as a dragon).

> or whatever
> else may affect it? If not, is anyone at least certain of which factors
> determine whether or not your god grants you an artifact? Thanks in
> advance.

The only critical factors once reconciled are the number of
existing artifacts (includes Quest one) and the number of prior
gifts.  The more gifts and artifacts, the gift rate drops
geometerically.



